{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/976557-the-arctic-suicides-it-s-not-the-dark-that-kills-you","id":976557,"title":"The Arctic Suicides: It's Not The Dark That Kills You","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-26T09:14:53-07:00","id":976557,"title":"The Arctic Suicides: It's Not The Dark That Kills You","content":"For those of you wondering what the Wendigo are facing other than Wyrmcreatures:<br /> <br /> &quot;The first death was on the night of Jan. 9.<br /> <br /> It was a Saturday. Pele Kristiansen spent the morning at home, drinking beers and hanging out with his older brother, which wasn't so unusual. There wasn't a lot of work in town. A lot of people drank. In the afternoon, they heard someone banging on their door, yelling.<br /> <br /> &quot;Polar bear! It's a polar bear!&quot;<br /> On the frozen fjord a couple of miles away, they could see the bear. Hunting in the Arctic \u2014 bears and reindeer and seals and birds \u2014 is at the core of Inuit life, even today.<br /> The polar bear was coming toward the town.<br /> A little drunk and really excited, Pele and his buddies fired up the motor on their fishing boat and nosed through the slushy ice in the harbor of their East Greenland village, Tiniteqilaaq, until they were as close as they could get. They got out of the boat, stood on the ice and pointed their rifles at the enormous animal.<br /> <br /> Among the Inuit, hunting a polar bear is a big deal. The bears have huge territories \u2014 to actually see one around Tiniteqilaaq was rare. And because of their size and ferocity, they're not easy to kill. It's usually a group effort, so according to tradition, the first four people to shoot it share the meat and the glory.<br /> That day, Pele shot the polar bear.<br /> And he was so happy.<br /> That evening, Pele went out drinking to celebrate.<br /> The next morning he was dead. He had killed himself. He was 22.<br /> Thirteen days later, in the next town over, a 15-year-old boy named Peter Pilanat killed himself in his grandparents' home. Peter and Pele didn't know each other, at least not well, but they had friends in common. In a place with only 3,000 people, Peter most certainly knew of Pele's death.<br /> <br /> Two suicides in less than two weeks. To the people in these small towns, it felt like the beginning of something bad, something sickeningly familiar. Something that had happened too many times in too many towns in Greenland. A cluster of suicides, inexplicable and indiscriminate, tearing its way through the youngest generation in a country that has the highest known suicide rate in the world.&quot;<br /> <br /> Read more:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.npr.org/sections/goatsandsoda/2016/04/21/474847921/the-arctic-suicides-its-not-the-dark-that-kills-you\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://media.npr.org/assets/img/2016/04/19/greenland-13_wide-2cf583392dc499f423f0141fadbfe40d38119e4d-s1400-c100.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.npr.org/sections/goatsandsoda/2016/04/21/474847921/the-arctic-suicides-its-not-the-dark-that-kills-you\" target=\"_blank\"> The Arctic Suicides: It's Not The Dark That Kills You </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.npr.org/sections/goatsandsoda/2016/04/21/474847921/the-arctic-suicides-its-not-the-dark-that-kills-you\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.npr.org/sections/goatsandsoda/2016/04/21/474847921/the-arctic-suicides-its-not-the-dark-that-kills-you </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Greenland has the world's highest suicide rate. And teen boys are at the highest risk. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":707,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","user":"etherial","date":". 09-26-2016, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:27:24-07:00","id":976563,"title":"","content":"I read this when it first came out and found it incredibly moving. While I'm not sure how to make it gameable in a tasteful way, it's nonetheless a great article.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T10:15:36-07:00","id":976598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/976557-the-arctic-suicides-it-s-not-the-dark-that-kills-you?p=976563#post976563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read this when it first came out and found it incredibly moving. While I'm not sure how to make it gameable in a tasteful way, it's nonetheless a great article.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pshaw, I say. Pshaw! You don't have to make a WtA scenario about this exact thing, but the themes of marginalized people suffering from suicide epidemics is not something that is unique to the Greenlandic Inuit. I think there are communities of Wendigo kin in the Americas who would likely have the very same issues.<br /> <br /> I just watched the Babadook this weekend and it got me thinking; banes and evil spirits are often used as a crass and obvious opponent. These spirits turn people into mutants and werewolves can just rip up the offenders in a paroxysm of anger... but I think spirits associated with loss, depression and alienation are things that should not be easily destroyed. Like the Babadook, these things can't be killed- just contained. You might destroy that avatar of the Nameless Angel of Despair, but treating your daughter's depression that called to the thing in the first place? Much harder.<br /> <br /> A rash of suicides in a dying town, awash in poverty and cheapbootleg liquor. The Wendigo have made certain that the wilderness and sacred places are safe- but now the enemy creeps into the hearts and minds of their kin, feeding on their numb misery and quiet desperation. Fixing a tiny, troubled mountain town is something that werewolves are not very good at, but even if they fail, it could make for a very poignant and touching story.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T15:40:12-07:00","id":976766,"title":"","content":"A good movie. A possibly more interesting story would involve a spiritual predator feeding off of European Alaskans which originally feed on the local Native Americans, including Wendigo Kinfolk, until they became too hard to find (there really are not enough Greenlanders, Inuit or European, for anything to bother with).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}